  "result": "Think of the model as a manager locked in an office who can only pass notes under the door.\n\nSay a student asks, \"Is the laser cutter free Friday?\" The manager can't check the calendar, so they write a note: \"Look up the laser cutter's bookings for Friday.\" An assistant outside, your program, reads the note, does the lookup and slips the result back under the door. The manager reads it and writes the reply to the student.\n\nSo the model never runs anything. It only writes a structured request, and your code decides whether and how to carry it out.\n\nThe analogy breaks in one place. The manager has to be told which requests the assistant can handle, and that list of tool descriptions is what you'll write for the makerspace assistant.",
